  "hints": [
    "Model the circle as a queue: 'skipping' a child means moving it from the front to the back.",
    "To eliminate the k-th child, move k-1 children from front to back, then remove the front. With k up to 10^9 you must not do k-1 moves each round.",
    "Only (k-1) mod (current size) moves matter, because a full lap returns the queue to the same order. That makes each round O(size) and the total O(n^2), fine for n = 3000."
  ],
  "editorial": "Keep the circle as a queue whose front is the child where counting starts. Eliminating the `k`-th child means rotating the queue by `k - 1` positions (front to back) and then popping the front.\n\nA full lap of `size` rotations changes nothing, so rotate only `(k - 1) mod size` times. Each round costs at most `size - 1` rotations, giving `O(n^2)` in total, which is fine for `n ≤ 3000`. (A Fenwick tree with k-th element search gets `O(n log n)`, but is not needed here.)",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n# simulate the circle with a queue\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// simulate the circle with a queue\n// readLine() returns the next input line (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    // simulate the circle with a queue\n    return 0;\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        // simulate the circle with a queue\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "from collections import deque\nn, k = map(int, input().split())\nq = deque(range(1, n + 1))\nout = []\nwhile q:\n    q.rotate(-((k - 1) % len(q)))\n    out.append(q.popleft())\nprint(' '.join(map(str, out)))\n",
    "javascript": "const [n, k] = readLine().trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nconst q = [];\nfor (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) q.push(i);\nlet head = 0, size = n;\nconst out = [];\nwhile (size > 0) {\n  const m = (k - 1) % size;\n  for (let i = 0; i < m; i++) q.push(q[head++]);\n  out.push(q[head++]);\n  size--;\n}\nconsole.log(out.join(' '));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        long k = sc.nextLong();\n        ArrayDeque<Integer> q = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) q.addLast(i);\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        while (!q.isEmpty()) {\n            long m = (k - 1) % q.size();\n            for (long i = 0; i < m; i++) q.addLast(q.pollFirst());\n            if (sb.length() > 0) sb.append(' ');\n            sb.append(q.pollFirst());\n        }\n        System.out.println(sb);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    deque<int> q;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) q.push_back(i);\n    bool first = true;\n    while (!q.empty()) {\n        long long m = (k - 1) % (long long)q.size();\n        for (long long i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            q.push_back(q.front());\n            q.pop_front();\n        }\n        if (!first) cout << ' ';\n        first = false;\n        cout << q.front();\n        q.pop_front();\n    }\n    cout << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n"
  }
